# Mandatory Engineering System Rule

This repository follows the canonical Engineering System.

Always read:
1. @AGENTS.md
2. @.engineering/project.yaml

Read only when relevant:
3. @.engineering/tests.yaml for implementation/debugging/testing
4. @.engineering/release.yaml for release/version/artifact work
5. only the relevant product specification/ADR/runbook/Engineering System standard

Then:
- classify the change and affected domains/contracts/security/operations
- inspect relevant implementation/tests
- make the smallest correct change
- run cheapest affected deterministic tests first
- keep ordinary PR validation fast
- do not duplicate equivalent native CI
- do not run a full release suite while a blocking deterministic regression exists
- add/retain durable regression coverage for bugs
- never weaken a valid test merely to obtain PASS
- never report unexecuted/skipped/blocked/historical evidence as current PASS
- never reuse release qualification evidence from another source HEAD

When explicitly resuming an existing workstream, use the repository-scoped active AI Work Packet and verify current Git state before acting. Do not load packets from unrelated repositories. Fail closed on missing or ambiguous packet selection.

Tool-specific rules may adapt syntax but must not weaken the Engineering System core.
